# superglue

Rust orchestration core at `projects/superglue/`. **All orchestration logic lives here** — bindings are thin FFI wrappers.

## Design docs (read in order)

Start at [`_docs/README.md`](_docs/README.md):

1. Vision → Architecture → Tool boundary & async
2. Protobuf/gRPC → Observability → Security
3. Roadmap → Ecosystem reference

## Binding parity

API or tool-boundary changes require updates in:

- [`superglue-py`](../superglue-py)
- [`superglue-js`](../superglue-js)
- [`superglue-kt`](../superglue-kt)

## Tool boundary

- JSON payloads across FFI — no opaque Python objects in the Rust core loop.
- JS: explicit JSON Schema per tool. Python: introspection at binding layer only.

## Feature flags (`Cargo.toml`)

| Feature | Purpose |
|---------|---------|
| `grpc` | gRPC server/client |
| `otlp` | OpenTelemetry export |
| `prometheus` | Metrics endpoint |
| `realtime` | Provider-agnostic realtime voice sessions (xAI WebSocket first) |

Gate optional deps behind features; keep default build lean.

## Testing

- Heavy Wiremock suite in `tests/`.
- Tool harness for offline scripted plans — prefer over live API in CI.

## Consumers

`loom`, `charlotte`, `loom-coms`, and all language bindings.
